From 57319e026639faa9c3896cfae74710f8ec740a44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:19:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Replace gnu-keyring.gpg with libextractor-keyring.pgp, the keyserver
copy of the key that signs releases
(D8423BCB326C7907033929C7939E6BE1E29FC3CC), because sqv cannot use the
old keyring: it holds 10 v3 (PGP 2) keys, which Sequoia does not parse,
so sqv rejects the whole file (GnuPG skips such keys silently). The
other certificates in it are dropped (541 certificates of other people).
Its Source line names the new file instead of
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnu-keyring.gpg, which is not what the file
holds any more.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore               |   1 -
 libextractor-keyring.pgp | 837 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libextractor.spec        |   4 +-
 sources                  |   1 -
 4 files changed, 840 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libextractor-keyring.pgp

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 9051c9d..5bc367c 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -24,7 +24,6 @@
 /libextractor-1.10.tar.gz.sig
 /libextractor-1.13.tar.gz
 /libextractor-1.13.tar.gz.sig
-/gnu-keyring.gpg
 /libextractor-1.14.tar.gz
 /libextractor-1.14.tar.gz.sig
 /libextractor-1.15.tar.gz
diff --git a/libextractor-keyring.pgp b/libextractor-keyring.pgp
